statement:
Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and $C$ a smooth connected curve over $k$ [def-sc-curves]; by [lem-sc-smooth-connected-curve-local-rings] $C$ is a Noetherian integral scheme with generic point $\eta$ and function field $k(C)=\mathcal O_{C,\eta}$ [def-sc-function-field], and for every closed point $P$ the local ring $\mathcal O_{C,P}\subseteq k(C)$ is a discrete valuation ring with normalized valuation $v_P:k(C)^*\to\mathbf Z$. Let $\mathcal L$ be an invertible $\mathcal O_C$-module [def-sc-invertible-module], and for each point $x$ let $\lambda_x:\mathcal L_x\to\mathcal L_\eta$ be the germ map of stalks [def-weil-pbc-module-stalk]; by [lem-sc-invertible-module-generic-stalk] $\mathcal L_x$ is free of rank one over $\mathcal O_{C,x}$, $\mathcal L_\eta$ is a one-dimensional $k(C)$-vector space, and $\lambda_x$ of a generator of $\mathcal L_x$ is a basis of $\mathcal L_\eta$. Let $s\in\mathcal L_\eta$, $s\neq0$. Then:

1. for every closed point $P$ and generators $e,e'$ of $\mathcal L_P$, the elements $g,g'\in k(C)^*$ with $s=g\,\lambda_P(e)=g'\,\lambda_P(e')$ satisfy $v_P(g)=v_P(g')$;
2. there are only finitely many closed points $P$ such that $v_P(g)\neq0$ for the element $g\in k(C)^*$ with $s=g\,\lambda_P(e)$, $e$ a generator of $\mathcal L_P$.
